.TH MAGNOLIE-HANDBUCH 1 "August 2026" "Magnolie Handbook 2.0.6" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
magnolie-handbuch \- open the Magnolie Organizer user handbook
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B magnolie-handbuch
.RI [ option ]
.RI [ \-\-sprache\  language ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Magnolie Handbook
opens the complete illustrated user guide for Magnolie Organizer. The handbook
can be browsed on screen, printed or exported as a PDF file.
.PP
Only one handbook window is opened per user session. Starting the command
again presents the existing window.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-sprache " " SPRACHE , " " \-\-language " " LANGUAGE
Use German (\fBde\fR), English (\fBen\fR), or the system language
(\fBsystem\fR) for this invocation. This selects command output before help
and the WebKit language of a newly opened window. Persisted settings are not
changed.
.TP
.BR \-\-pot " [" DATEI "]", " " \-\-pot-template " [" FILE "]"
Generate a reproducible gettext template and exit. With no file argument,
write \fBmagnolie-handbuch.pot\fR in the current directory; otherwise write
to the specified path. The absolute output path is printed on success.
.TP
.BR \-\-hilfe , " " \-\-help
Show a short command overview.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MAGNOLIE_HANDBUCH_WEB
Use an alternative directory containing the handbook interface. Intended for
development and testing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR magnolie-organizer (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Maik Walter.
